//! Shared help paragraphs. Values describe policy; validation checks their limits.
pub(crate) const COPY: &str = "Copy uses the inactive disk panel directory for a blank destination. If the other pane shows an archive, enter a disk destination or use Tree. F5 from disk to a ZIP instead opens Update ZIP.\nAsk before replacing is the default: directories merge and conflicting files offer Replace, Skip, Replace all, Skip all or Cancel. All choices apply only to this transfer.\nExplicit Refuse rejects existing top-level destinations before changes. Explicit Skip leaves existing top-level files and directories untouched, without merging. Skipped sources remain.\nCheck free disk space estimates source lengths; overhead and later changes can still cause errors. Verify disk writes reads back staged bytes before publication. Remove source files forces verification and removes sources only after the copied batch succeeds.\nF4 opens destination history; Tree chooses a directory without navigating either panel. Esc cancels; completed work remains. Append, refresh and description copying are unavailable.";
pub(crate) const MOVE: &str = "Move/rename uses the inactive disk panel directory; Shift+F6 uses the active directory. Relative paths use that base. A single item may use a new name; multiple items need an existing directory.\nAsk before replacing is the default: directories merge and conflicting files offer Replace, Skip, Replace all, Skip all or Cancel for this transfer only. Skipped sources remain.\nExplicit Refuse rejects existing top-level destinations before changes. Explicit Skip leaves existing top-level files and folders untouched, without merging.\nNative exclusive rename is preferred where possible. Verification uses staged copying and guarded source cleanup. Free-space checking applies when copying is required. Remove source files is selected and locked.\nF4 opens history; Tree chooses a disk directory. Esc cancels; completed moves remain. Append, refresh and description copying are unavailable.";
pub(crate) const VIEWING:&str="F2 toggles wrapping; F7 searches and Shift+F7 finds the next match. Go to accepts source lines, or byte offsets in Hex. Regular disk files above 64 MiB stream through bounded windows; long lines are clipped. Archive previews and formatted Markdown remain bounded. F8 selects reading encoding; bounded viewers reinterpret loaded bytes. Editor snapshots have no reading encoding. F6 switches Markdown/source; F5 returns to the source editor preview. Search uses displayed text; Markdown Go to uses source lines. Links and images do not open automatically.";
pub(crate) const SAVE_FORMAT:&str="File → Save with encoding in the editor converts on save. F2 preserves encoding, BOM and mixed line endings. Unrepresentable characters block saving; choose UTF-8 to retain them. The editor supports 64 MiB / 1,000,000 lines. Save As asks before replacing an existing file.";
